    "--agent",
    "build",
    "--format",
    "json",
    "Complete this repository task: `scan(pattern)` splits a glob into a static base and a glob remainder, and reports flags\ndescribing what it found. It currently mis-scans negated extglobs.\n\nA leading `!` negates a pattern, so `scan('!a/b/*.js')` reports prefix '!', start 1, base 'a/b',\nglob '*.js' and negated true. But `!(` opens a *negated extglob*, which is part of the pattern\nand must not be consumed as a negation prefix: `scan('!(a|b)')` must report prefix '', start 0,\nbase '', glob '!(a|b)', isExtglob true, negatedExtglob true and negated false. Today it reports\nthe extglob as a negation instead.\n\nFix `lib/scan.js` so both forms are classified correctly, without disturbing the base/glob split\nfor ordinary patterns, `./` prefixes, braces, brackets, globstars or escaped `!` characters. The\n`nonegate` option must still suppress negation while leaving extglob detection intact.\nWork only in the current repository. Do not push, open a PR, deploy, or access secrets.\nMake the smallest correct change and run relevant local checks."
  ],
